### §6.3 Selection-bias correction (mandatory — the probe over-samples)

The three probed goals are **the most heavily instrumented goals in the entire corpus**.
Measured across all 42 sealed-goal reviews and all 176 debt records:

| Property | Corpus rate | Effect on the probe |
|---|---|---|
| Has the rich CER-4 twin in `docs/` | **4 / 42 (9.5%)** | All three probed goals are in that 4. |
| Has a RESOLVED/closed debt record (Outcome source) | **2 / 176 debts** | Both belong to probed goals (DEBT-0002, DEBT-0003). |
| Review mentions a trade-off (any casing) | **0 / 42 (0%)** | Confirms §6.2 is not a small-sample artifact. |
| Review contains any 40+ hex char (artifact hash) | **0 / 42 (0%)** | `EvidenceRef` hashing is categorically absent. |
| Review hints at a rejected/considered alternative | **9 / 42 (21%)** | Probe's 0.67 Option rate is ~3× the corpus rate. |
| Review names ≥1 test id | **31 / 42 (74%)** | Roughly representative. |
| Review carries an explicit date | **42 / 42 (100%)** | `valid_from` is safe. |
| Debt records on the machine friction template | **128 / 176 (73%)** | Uniform, goal-joined, parseable — see §7.3. |

Re-scoring the 38 goals that have **only** the `reviews/tasks/` checklist form yields a
fidelity of **31.5 / 72 = 0.44**. Corpus-weighted projection:

```
(4 × 0.653 + 38 × 0.4375) / 42 = 0.458  →  corpus_projected_loss_ratio = 0.54
```

**The headline 0.35 is a best-case ceiling, not a typical value.** Any S1 backfill plan
must budget against 0.54, not 0.35.

