## §10 Assumptions surfaced and residual risks

Surfaced per the DESIGN-stage evidence requirement (assumptions stated, perspectives
covered, no orphan or gap). Each is falsifiable.

| # | Assumption made by this probe | If wrong |
|:--:|---|---|
| **P1** | E/P/A scored 1.0/0.5/0.0 is a fair loss metric. A different weighting moves the headline number. | The *shape* (§6.2) is weighting-independent: `TradeOff` is A/P/A and `Constraint`/`Component` are E/E/E under any scheme. The verdict rests on the shape, not the scalar. |
| **P2** | The five assigned fields (§2.2) are legitimately excluded from the denominator. | Including them yields loss ≈ 0.26 — a *better* number. The exclusion is conservative and cannot flatter the result. |
| **P3** | Hand-extraction by a careful reader approximates what a built extractor achieves. | **This is the probe's weakest point.** A human resolved implicit trade-off axes and cross-artifact joins that a parser would miss; an LLM-based extractor is non-deterministic where a human was consistent. Machine fidelity is likely **below** 0.65. §9.2's per-field `fidelity` tag exists so the real number is measured, not assumed. |
| **P4** | Three goals generalize. | Explicitly **not assumed** — §6.3 corrects for it across all 42 reviews and all 176 debt records, and the corrected projection (0.54) is the one the delivery plan should budget against. |
| **P5** | Missing L06/L04/L11 artifacts are producible going forward. | If PAEOS continues to skip L06 on Trace-B work (§7.1), `TradeOff` stays at ~0 and C3's re-ordering becomes permanent rather than temporary — `tradeoff_precedents` would never become buildable. R1 is the mitigation; it is non-blocking only because C3 removes the dependency. |
| **P6** | The 128 friction records are extraction-worthy. | Not scored into the loss ratio — deliberately excluded, since none of the three probed goals used that template. It is upside, not a load-bearing assumption. |

**Residual risks carried** (not eliminated): machine-vs-human extraction gap (P3);
permanent `TradeOff` scarcity if L06 conformance is not fixed (P5); corpus sample bias,
which SAEOS-1 §9/A4 already carries and which §6.3 now quantifies at the artifact level.

**Perspectives covered.** Builder (§9 buildability), Architect (§7.4 emission point, §9.1
component graph), Risk Officer (§8.3 blocking conditions, §10 residuals), Replay (§9.2
auditable `source_ref`, §2.2 reproducible scoring), Maintainer (§7.1/§7.2 producer-side
debts, R1/R2), Adversary (§6.3 self-directed selection-bias correction, P3 self-criticism).
Security is out of scope for an extraction probe and is routed to Ω6, untouched here.

**No orphans.** Every §4.3 node type is scored in all three goals; every §4.2 field is
either scored or explicitly excluded with a reason (§2.2); every blocking condition traces
to a numbered finding in §7; every finding traces to a cited artifact.

